/S /H2
/P 68 0 R
/T (Guided by this year's conference theme, "Engineering Stability in an Age of Volatility," delegates are encouraged to explore how gender-responsive policies can serve as powerful tools for building resilient societies in an increasingly uncertain world. Today's international landscape is shaped by complex and interconnected challenges, including armed conflict, geopolitical tensions, economic instability, climate change, public health crises, forced displacement, and rapid technological transformation. These challenges often affect women and girls disproportionately, widening existing inequalities while simultaneously highlighting the indispensable role they play in fostering recovery, innovation, and sustainable peace.)
/E (Guided by this year's conference theme, "Engineering Stability in an Age of Volatility," delegates are encouraged to explore how gender-responsive policies can serve as powerful tools for building resilient societies in an increasingly uncertain world. Today's international landscape is shaped by complex and interconnected challenges, including armed conflict, geopolitical tensions, economic instability, climate change, public health crises, forced displacement, and rapid technological transformation. These challenges often affect women and girls disproportionately, widening existing inequalities while simultaneously highlighting the indispensable role they play in fostering recovery, innovation, and sustainable peace.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
199 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 68 0 R
/T (Delegates are therefore invited to examine how governments, international organizations, and local stakeholders can integrate gender perspectives into policymaking to strengthen national and global resilience. Discussions may focus on improving women's participation in peacebuilding and conflict resolution, promoting equal access to education and economic opportunities, addressing gender-based violence during humanitarian crises, closing digital divides in an era of technological advancement, and ensuring that climate adaptation and disaster response strategies are inclusive and equitable.)
/E (Delegates are therefore invited to examine how governments, international organizations, and local stakeholders can integrate gender perspectives into policymaking to strengthen national and global resilience. Discussions may focus on improving women's participation in peacebuilding and conflict resolution, promoting equal access to education and economic opportunities, addressing gender-based violence during humanitarian crises, closing digital divides in an era of technological advancement, and ensuring that climate adaptation and disaster response strategies are inclusive and equitable.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
