/P 70 0 R
/E (Today, the convergence of geopolitical instability, economic volatility, and accelerating environmental degradation has pushed fragile states into unprecedented levels of vulnerability. In regions spanning from the African Sahel and Horn of Africa to Haiti and South Asia, climate change now acts as a primary "threat multiplier." Severe prolonged droughts, desertification, and catastrophic flooding destroy local agricultural livelihoods, forcing mass internal displacement and sparking fierce armed disputes over remaining arable land and clean water sources. Rural women, who make up the majority of agricultural labor in many developing economies, find themselves caught directly in the crosshairs of these resource conflicts, facing heightened risks of physical violence, severe food insecurity, and economic loss without legal protections or formal representation in local resource management boards.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
