1055 0 obj
<<
/Title (At the heart of UN Women's mission is the recognition that gender equality is not only a fundamental human right but also a cornerstone of sustainable development, peace, and global prosperity. Societies that empower women and girls benefit from stronger economies, more effective institutions, healthier communities, and greater social cohesion. Conversely, gender inequality exacerbates poverty, fuels instability, and limits the ability of nations to respond effectively to global challenges. For this reason, UN Women places gender equality at the center of efforts to achieve lasting development and resilience.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 960 0 R
/Prev 1027 0 R
/Next 1071 0 R
>>
endobj
1056 0 obj
<<
/Title <>
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 960 0 R
/Prev 1072 0 R
/Next 1028 0 R
>>
endobj
1057 0 obj
<<
/Title (When armed conflicts break out or climate disasters devastate communities, standard physical and social infrastructures collapse rapidly. In these volatile environments, basic survival often falls squarely onto the shoulders of women, who take on the burden of securing clean water, gathering scarce food supplies, managing healthcare needs, and maintaining community cohesion. Despite performing these critical roles on the ground, women are almost entirely excluded when international organizations, peace negotiators, and local governments gather to design post-crisis recovery policies, allocate humanitarian funding, or restructure governance.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1030 0 R
/Next 1073 0 R
>>
endobj
1058 0 obj
<<
/Title (Implementing "gender-responsive strategies" requires a fundamental shift in how the international community approaches crisis management. Rather than simply delivering short-term humanitarian assistance, gender-responsive policymaking intentionally addresses the underlying structural inequalities that make women more vulnerable to crises in the first place. This means restructuring legal systems to guarantee women equal land ownership, establishing financial channels that grant female entrepreneurs credit after a collapse, and creating formal seats for women at governance tables during crisis recovery. When policies actively empower women to direct resource management and community stabilization, entire regions demonstrate significantly higher resilience, lower rates of civil unrest, and more equitable economic recovery following major shocks.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1030 0 R
/Prev 1073 0 R
>>
endobj
1059 0 obj
<<
/Title (This groundbreaking resolution formally created the Women, Peace, and Security \(WPS\) Agenda, marking the first time the international community officially acknowledged that sustainable global peace is mathematically impossible to achieve without the active, equal participation of women in conflict prevention, peace negotiations, and post-conflict governance.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 961 0 R
/Prev 1031 0 R
/Next 1032 0 R
>>
endobj
1060 0 obj
<<
/Title (Conflict, disasters, and displacement expose women and girls to heightened risks of violence, exploitation, and limited access to essential services. This topic focuses on policies that strengthen protection, provide education and healthcare, and create opportunities for economic independence.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1034 0 R
>>
endobj
