1070 0 obj
<<
/Title (Our committee will address urgent issues of resilience and gender equality. I encourage you to bring respect, passion, and collaboration to every discussion. Every voice matters, and the best resolutions come from diverse perspectives working in unity. I look forward to guiding our work and making this conference both productive and memorable.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1025 0 R
/Prev 1069 0 R
/Next 1054 0 R
>>
endobj
1071 0 obj
<<
/Title (Guided by this year's conference theme, "Engineering Stability in an Age of Volatility," delegates are encouraged to explore how gender-responsive policies can serve as powerful tools for building resilient societies in an increasingly uncertain world. Today's international landscape is shaped by complex and interconnected challenges, including armed conflict, geopolitical tensions, economic instability, climate change, public health crises, forced displacement, and rapid technological transformation. These challenges often affect women and girls disproportionately, widening existing inequalities while simultaneously highlighting the indispensable role they play in fostering recovery, innovation, and sustainable peace.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 960 0 R
/Prev 1055 0 R
/Next 1077 0 R
>>
endobj
1072 0 obj
<<
/Title (Through constructive dialogue, diplomacy, collaboration, and evidence-based policymaking, participants will have the opportunity to develop innovative and practical solutions that address both immediate challenges and long-term structural inequalities. Delegates are encouraged to engage in respectful debate, consider diverse perspectives, and work toward consensus-driven resolutions that reflect the principles of equality, inclusion, human dignity, and international cooperation.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 960 0 R
/Prev 1077 0 R
/Next 1056 0 R
>>
endobj
1073 0 obj
<<
/Title <>
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1030 0 R
/Prev 1057 0 R
/Next 1058 0 R
>>
endobj
1074 0 obj
<<
/Title (Legal and financial barriers continue to prevent many women from owning property, inheriting assets, and accessing credit or financial services. Delegates should consider reforms that promote equal economic rights and enable women to participate fully in national economies. .)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1061 0 R
>>
endobj
